A||||1||roadrunner||How do you repair trunk lock?||||1||
Z||000000||roadrunner||07-30-2000||05:09 PM||||I replaced the black plastic spring loaded door on my '86 SE only to have it break again in 6 months. I found a permanent repair on a Chevette!  On an '81 or '82 Chevette, the stainless steel end cap with the spring loaded door and the stainless steel bezel that attached it the to the trunk lock are the same part as the plastic ones on Fieros! Find these parts at any salvage yard.  Remove the trunk lock on the Fiero, remove the broken plastic, and install the stainless steel parts.  Just bend the tab on the stainless bezel over the ears on the Fiero lock and reinstall the lock in your Fiero.  Permanent fix.   Won't break again.||||reg||1
Z||000001||84 Indy||07-30-2000||05:57 PM||||I just bought a trunck lock from The Fiero Store .  I is black and the part you are talking about is metal.||||reg||10
